Read the macOS version through sysctl rather than private CoreFoundation

MacOSVersionComponents() read the system version from
_CFCopySystemVersionDictionary() and its _kCFSystemVersion*Key constants. Those
are private CoreFoundation interfaces, and although they are declared as weak
imports, referencing them is enough to leave their symbols in every binary that
links crashpad. App Store review rejects such binaries under guideline 2.5.1.

kern.osproductversion and kern.osversion carry the same values and are public;
MacOSVersionNumber() right above already reads the former. The product name has
no sysctl counterpart and only feeds the human readable version string, so it is
derived from the version itself. The product version extra is dropped, being
absent from sysctl and normally unset anyway.

